      "content": "Don’t worry, the situation is straightforward. Since the crate moves at a constant speed, its acceleration is zero, so the sum of the forces along the incline must cancel out.\n\nAlong the slope we have three forces:\n• The component of gravity down the plane, $mg\\sin\\theta$\n• The kinetic friction force, $40\\,\\text{N}$, also down the plane\n• The applied force $F$ acting up the plane.\n\nBecause the motion is steady, \\(F_{net}=0\\).\n\n**Question:** Write the equation that represents the balance of forces along the incline (choose a positive direction and include all three forces)."
